Installed kubuntu-25.10-desktop-amd64-A as VM on virtual hard disk.
I upgraded kubuntu-25.10-desktop-amd64-A to version 26.04 LTS.
Mounted and installed Guest Additions ()


I attempted to install neon-unstable-dev-20260831-1139, but it crashed during installation.  I removed the VM.

I attempted to install neon-user-desktop-20260903-0454.  Seems to have succeeded.
There was a System upgrade.  I installed it.
Lost the window. See below for how I was able to get it to be visible again.


I attempted to install fedora-kde-desktop-live-44-1_7_x86_64 .  While the install appeared to succeed, the VM wouldn't start from the virtual hard disk.
I reinstalled.
I had to unmount the virtual CD.
There were security updates, which turned out to be a System Upgrade just like kubuntu and neon.
During the upgrade, I couldn't see the VM window although it showed up in the taskbar, grouped with neon's VM window.
FOund that if I hovered over the grouped VM windows on the task bar, then moved the mouse over the missing window, then right clicked, selected More and chose "Move", I could move the window into a visible area.


